{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"targeted-cultish-dormouse","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nWhen the store wedges (dirty tracker tree, stale locks, stranded merge state), today's tooling is partial: `rebar fsck` checks event integrity but does not report the dirty-tree class that caused the recent P0 wedges (tracked working-tree deletions of store artifacts, untracked regenerable compaction leftovers, orphaned lock files, orphaned `.tmp-event-*`); `rebar tracker-maintenance --clean` handles only a stranded index and foreign worktree paths (verified: its `_stranded_paths`/`_foreign_worktree_paths` scans reported 0 findings while the store sat wedged with 119 tracked `.archived` deletions); the documented recovery for the live wedges was ad-hoc raw git under the write lock, recorded by hand on tickets 6ccc-0577-198c-44fa / e72e-259d-5ee7-4e73. Operators (and agents) need one sanctioned, non-destructive door: fsck DETECTS the class, doctor --repair HEALS it.\n\n## Approach\nDetection: add a tracker-dirty check to the fsck surface (src/rebar/_commands/fsck_tracker_health.py, which already owns tracker-level health lines) that classifies `git status --porcelain` output into: (1) tracked deletions of store artifacts restorable from HEAD, (2) untracked regenerable compaction leftovers (`*-SNAPSHOT.json`, `*.retired` whose retired-source is already folded), (3) orphaned `.tmp-event-*` (never auto-touched — named for manual triage), plus lock-artifact staleness reported via the existing doctor_locks scan. Each class gets a distinct finding string and JSON field so agents can act programmatically.\nRepair: extend `rebar doctor --repair` (src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py's existing scan/repair_finding registry pattern) with repair actions that run under the store write lock (rebar._store.lock.write_lock): restore class-1 paths via `git checkout --` (non-destructive; bytes exist at HEAD), move class-2 paths into the quarantine directory established by change 1757 (`<git-common-dir>/reconverge-quarantine/<utc-ts>/` — move, never delete), and leave class-3 untouched while printing their paths. After healing, invoke the existing reconverge entry (rebar._store.sync.reconverge) so a previously wedged store converges in the same command. Raw git here is the sanctioned exception: it goes through the store seam (gitutil.run_git) inside a lock-guarded repair command, exactly the pattern tracker-maintenance already uses, and every action is recorded in the doctor output. Positive rationale: doctor already owns scan-classify-repair with typed findings; extending its registry avoids inventing a second repair CLI.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/_commands/fsck_tracker_health.py — tracker-dirty classification (text + JSON).\n- src/rebar/_commands/doctor.py — new finding types + repair actions under the write lock; post-repair reconverge call.\n- tests/unit/test_doctor_dirty_tree.py (new) — seeded-wedge end-to-end coverage.\n- docs/user-guide.md — document the new fsck findings and doctor repairs.\n\n## Testing\n- Happy path: fixture tracker seeded with all three classes plus a diverged origin; `rebar fsck` names each class; `rebar doctor --repair` restores class 1, quarantines class 2 (bytes preserved), leaves class 3 in place, and the store converges (ahead/behind 0/0, `git status` clean except class 3).\n- Failure/edge: doctor --repair on a CLEAN store makes zero changes and zero commits (idempotent); a locked store (write lock held by a live process) makes doctor wait/skip per existing lock semantics rather than repairing unlocked; class-3 files are byte-identical after the run.\n- JSON contract: fsck --output json carries the per-class counts and paths.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `rebar fsck` on a seeded dirty tracker reports each class with a distinct finding id, and clean stores report none; checked by the new test.\n- [ ] `rebar doctor --repair` heals a seeded wedge end-to-end (tree clean apart from `.tmp-event-*`, merge converged, no event bytes lost — quarantine holds moved files); checked by the end-to-end test.\n- [ ] Repair runs entirely under the store write lock and never deletes a file (moves or restores only); checked by asserting quarantine contents and lock acquisition in the test.\n- [ ] `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean; lands via Gerrit (LLM-Review +1 AND Verified +1) before close.","id":"c925-7669-ded8-43a3","parent_id":"fb8a-7363-e406-4e36","priority":1,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"fsck detects the dirty-tree/stale-lock wedge class; doctor --repair heals it under the write lock"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1786677403008700001,"uuid":"86314267-3311-4da0-b762-f71f07544032"}